  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "For which of the following situations can the distribution of the sample proportion $\\overset{^}{\\,p}$ be approximated as\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\,p}∼N(p,\\frac{p(1-p)}{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the population proportion?\n\nI. A sample of size $n=16$ from a population of size $N=100$ in which $25%$ of the population has a particular characteristic.\n\nII. A sample of size $n=32$ from a population of size $N=1\\,000$ in which $10%$ of the population has a particular characteristic.\n\nIII. A sample of size $n=32$  from a population of size $N=1\\,000$ in which $75%$ of the population has a particular characteristic.",
